Third-party components redistributed in this repository
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The targets are deliberately vulnerable applications. Some of them vendor a
third-party library so that the target builds and runs without reaching a package
registry at image-build time. Those components are listed here with the licence they
are distributed under; each retains whatever notice its licence requires.

  Vue                3.5.13   MIT
                     targets/blog/web/dist/assets/vue.global.prod-3.5.13.js
                     Copyright (c) 2018-present Yuxi (Evan) You and Vue contributors.
                     The upstream banner is retained verbatim in the file.

  htmx               2.0.4    Zero-Clause BSD (0BSD)
                     targets/intranet/hub/static/js/htmx.min.js
                     0BSD grants use, copying, modification and distribution with no
                     conditions and no attribution requirement. Listed here for
                     inventory rather than obligation.

Dependencies resolved at build time from a package registry — npm, PyPI, Maven
Central, NuGet — are not redistributed here and are not listed. Their versions are
pinned exactly in each target's manifest, deliberately: several planted flaws depend
on a specific version behaving a specific way, and an unpinned dependency silently
repairs the vulnerability it was chosen for.

